# {{project.title}}

Static site built with Astro, deployed to S3 and CloudFront. Pages and components are `.astro`
files that ship no JavaScript by default; React islands with MUI are available for the parts of a
page that need to be interactive.

## Local development

```
pnpm install
pnpm dev
```
{%- if contactForm %}

The contact form posts to `/api/contact`. To exercise it locally, run the intake next to Astro in a
second terminal; Astro proxies `/api` to it and the email it would send is printed:

```
pnpm dev:contact
```

reCAPTCHA is skipped locally unless you export `PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY` and
`RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY` for a key that lists `localhost` as an allowed domain.
{%- endif %}

## Build

```
pnpm build
```

`pnpm build` runs `astro build` and then `scripts/seo-check.ts`. A failed check aborts the build,
so nothing is deployed.

## How this site is structured

**`src/seo/routes.ts` is the single source of truth for every URL.** Titles, meta descriptions,
the primary navigation and the sitemap all read from it. A page passes its path to `Layout` and
the registry supplies the rest; there is no `title` prop. A page whose path is not registered
fails the build.

**`src/theme/tokens.ts` holds every color, font and size.** `Layout` emits them as CSS custom
properties (`--color-brand`, `--size-radius`, ...), and stylesheets use those. A React island that
needs an MUI theme builds it from the same object:

```tsx
import { createTheme } from "@mui/material/styles";
import { tokens } from "../theme/tokens.js";

export const theme = createTheme({
    palette: { primary: { main: tokens.color.brand }, text: { primary: tokens.color.ink } },
    typography: { fontFamily: tokens.font.sans },
});
```

Islands live in `src/components/*.tsx` and need a `client:*` directive where they are used, for
example `<SearchBox client:visible />`. Prefer `.astro` for anything that does not need to react
to input after the page loads.

**`src/seo/redirects.json` maps old URLs to new ones** (`{ "/about.php": "/about/" }`). When a
site replaces an older one, every URL that has links or search ranking pointing at it belongs here.
CloudFront answers them with a 301, matching the path case-insensitively and keeping the query
string. A target may also be a full URL on another site.

**`src/styles/global.css` holds element defaults** (type scale, links, focus ring, reduced motion)
and a few layout classes. Components style themselves in scoped `<style>` blocks.

## What the build asserts

`scripts/seo-check.ts` fails the build on any of the following:

- a page with no title, or a title or description still carrying scaffold text
- two pages sharing a title or a meta description
- a missing canonical link, or one that is not on the environment's site URL
- a page whose `<h1>` is empty in the static HTML
- a sitemap whose URL count disagrees with the registry, or a registry entry with no page
- a 404 page missing its heading or its noindex tag
- a `robots.txt` that lets crawlers into a non-production build, or blocks them in production
- a page carrying more CSS than the budget, counting inline styles and linked stylesheets
- an internal link that does not resolve to a built page or file
- a color literal anywhere in `src` outside `src/theme/tokens.ts`
- a redirect in `src/seo/redirects.json` that lands on a missing page, chains into another
  redirect, or hides a page that exists
